    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that. but sometimes it feels like the infection just sneaks up on you even when you're being careful with the cleaning. like you think it's fine one minute and then the next she's looking really rough. is there anything else i should know about how these things can just hide and then suddenly pop up? maybe certain environmental factors that make it more likely to happen?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Infections can certainly be sneaky, and indeed, several factors can contribute to a seemingly sudden outbreak. Dusty or dusty environments increase the risk, as brushing against the mucous membrane in the respiratory system can introduce bacteria. Humidity levels can also impact the likelihood of infection; too little or too much can weaken the animal's natural defenses. Additionally, overcrowded living conditions may facilitate the spread of pathogens. A compromised immune system – perhaps due to recent stress, such as a fever or illness – can also make your heifer more susceptible to infection. Regularly disinfecting the environment, keeping your animal hydrated, and ensuring it's not overcrowded will help mitigate these risks. Again, timeliness in consulting with your veterinarian if you suspect any problems is crucial.",
      "source": "target",
